<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Tier 1 - the public contract of the Tenancy platform module (docs/architecture/modules.md 4).

    Everything another module may know about tenancy lives here: the identifiers and states of the
    tenant registry (B-05); the tenancy kernel types (B-06.1a) - TenantAccess, TenantScope,
    TenantAccessReason, SchemaVersion, CoreSchemaVersion, InstalledPackages and
    TenantRoutingViolationException; and from B-06.1/B-06.3 onward ITenantConnectionResolver and
    ITenantDbContextFactory<T>. The implementation, including the catalog DbContext, is internal to
    Aurora.Platform.Tenancy.

    A *.Contracts project references Aurora.SharedKernel and Aurora.Documents.Canonical and nothing
    else (solution-layout.md 2, fitness rule L2). No EF, no Npgsql, no DI, no logging.

    The InternalsVisibleTo grants below are the whole of ADR-0007 3.4's "only Aurora.Platform.Tenancy
    may construct one": TenantAccess and TenantScope have internal constructors, and internal reaches
    exactly these two assemblies - the tenancy module, which will hold the scope factory (B-06.3),
    and its unit-test assembly, which proves the type surface. TenantAccessConstructionTests asserts
    this list as an exact set, so a third grant is a red test rather than a quiet widening.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Aurora.Platform.Tenancy.Contracts</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Aurora.SharedKernel\Aurora.SharedKernel.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Aurora.Platform.Tenancy" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Aurora.Platform.Tenancy.UnitTests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
